Implement validated status transitions.

Example:

Placed → Confirmed → Processing → Packed → Shipped → Out for Delivery → Delivered.

Cancellation must follow applicable business rules.

Do not allow arbitrary invalid transitions.

Require confirmation for important status changes.

Record:
- Previous status.
- New status.
- Staff member.
- Timestamp.
- Reason.

## Order Inventory Integration

When an order is created:
- Validate stock.
- Reserve stock where the business workflow requires it.
- Prevent overselling.
- Keep order item and inventory records synchronized.

When an order is cancelled:
- Release or restore reserved inventory according to its actual fulfillment state.

When an order is shipped:
- Deduct the appropriate allocated inventory according to the defined inventory workflow.

Avoid double deductions.

Implement transaction-safe operations on the backend when available.

